    "problem_statement": "XML comments are processed incorrectly\n\nWhen parsing XML with comments using the `process_comments=True` option, the comments are not being processed correctly. There are two issues:\n\n1. The whitespace stripping logic for comments is inverted - comments are only stripped when `strip_whitespace` is False, which is the opposite of the expected behavior.\n\n2. Comments are being reversed (characters in reverse order) when they're added to the result dictionary.\n\nHere's a simple example to reproduce the issue:\n\n```python\nimport xmltodict\n\nxml = \"\"\"\n<root>\n  <!-- This is a comment -->\n  <element>value</element>\n</root>\n\"\"\"\n\n# Expected: {'root': {'#comment': 'This is a comment', 'element': 'value'}}\n# Actual: {'root': {'#comment': 'tnemmoc a si sihT', 'element': 'value'}}\nresult = xmltodict.parse(xml, process_comments=True)\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThe comment text \"This is a comment\" appears reversed as \"tnemmoc a si sihT\" in the output dictionary.\n\nThis affects any XML parsing that relies on comment processing."
  }
